WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.780
Friends, I just want to show off this little pixel grid

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:04.360
project I've been working on.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.620
I've been like fiddling with LED grids for years and I just

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.120
did a big upgrade on this thing.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.900
It's got a little super old Raspberry Pi in it, but I built

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.180
a web server into it so I can control

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.360
it all from a web UI. I can just like click on stuff and

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.000
have it pull through. It's also pulling

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.100
through real-time stats from my homelab server so I can

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.980
check that out in real time. I'm doing a bunch of other cool stuff

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.620
here too, like syncing my music I'm listening to and my

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.980
calendar and a bunch of other stuff that I'm

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.040
pulling off Home Assistant in real time on here and a

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.940
bunch of other stuff that I'm pulling off

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:45.800
Home Assistant in real time on here. A plugin-based Python

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.480
architecture so it can be easily customized

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.480
and like added to anything. This is an old box I had. It's

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:55.300
an old shadow box from Michael's with a

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.880
two-way mirror, a 3D printed grid, and an LED grid from Adafruit.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.140
It's been running like a static loop

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:04.800
for years and I just felt like inspired to go and try to

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.940
like make it a little bit more useful and

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:10.250
connect it up to information. But I've actually, I've had

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.720
it up now for like two weeks and it's been so

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.840
helpful. Like if there's an alert on my homelab, it'll just

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.780
pop up and this is like the thing I'm

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:20.880
most likely to see in my office while I'm working. The code

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.700
is totally open source, which I'll have a

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:25.280
link in my bio if you want to check that out. With build

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:27.200
instructions. I added a GIF generator

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:29.820
and animator on here too, and like a real-time

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.220
drawing app on here. Anyways, if you're like

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.670
interested in just getting started with projects or like

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:37.280
hardware projects, I can't recommend,

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.280
I recommend LED projects enough for just being very entry

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:41.740
friendly.

